    // an optimisation.
    //
    // "If an account exists for that email, a reset link is on its way" is the
    // right answer and is returned either way — but only ONE of the two branches
    // used to open an SMTP conversation before answering. A known address took
    // as long as the mail server did; an unknown one returned after a single
    // indexed SELECT. The wording revealed nothing and the clock revealed
    // everything, one sample per address, which is a working account-enumeration
    // oracle against a hosting provider's whole customer list. Detaching the send
    // leaves the two branches differing by one INSERT.
    //
    // Nothing is lost by not waiting: the result was already discarded, and the
    // customer was never told whether it worked. Failures are logged, and the
    // rejection is swallowed so a dead mail server can never take the process
    // down through an unhandled rejection.
    //
    // `mayDeliverTo` consults the notification policy, which classifies
    // `password_reset` as CRITICAL and returns true without even loading the
