1	/**
2	 * Data layer for the platform-wide Live Ops monitor (/admin/monitor).
3	 *
4	 * This is a v1 built entirely on data the platform ALREADY collects — it adds
5	 * no new sampling, no new schema. Three real sources are fused into one feed:
6	 *
7	 *   1. Node utilization (`lib/node-capacity.ts` allNodeUtil) — CPU/RAM/DISK for
8	 *      Proxmox compute nodes, ACCOUNTS/DISK for hosting nodes. CPU/RAM are
9	 *      queried LIVE from Proxmox on every call (no caching) — this is the one
10	 *      genuinely real-time number in the feed. DISK is the pool's live status
11	 *      too. This is the exact function that already powers the node-capacity
12	 *      warning banner and the Nodes admin page.
13	 *   2. Recent actions — the `Job` table (every VPS + game-server provisioning/
14	 *      power/backup/etc. action) fused with `HostingTask` (the equivalent queue
15	 *      for shared-hosting accounts, which do NOT create Job rows — see
16	 *      worker/hosting.ts). Together these cover every server kind the platform
17	 *      runs. Zero new instrumentation: both tables are written by the existing
18	 *      action/worker code on every real operation.
19	 *   3. Per-server resource state — `Server.bwInBytes/bwOutBytes` (metered by
20	 *      lib/bandwidth.ts on the worker's 10-minute sweep), the latest
21	 *      `ServerDiskSample` row (same sweep, guest-agent disk usage), and for
22	 *      shared hosting `HostingAccount.diskUsedMB`/`serveHttpOk`/`serveHttpsOk`
23	 *      (hostingUsageSweep / hostingHealthSweep). These are real but NOT
24	 *      per-request-live — they refresh on the worker's cadence (~10 min) and
25	 *      each row's own timestamp is returned so the UI can say exactly how
26	 *      stale it is instead of implying it's instantaneous.
27	 *
28	 * WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO: there is no live per-VM CPU/RAM series
29	 * (Proxmox reports that per-VM, but nothing persists it, and polling every VM's
30	 * `/qemu/{vmid}/status/current` on every fleet-wide poll would multiply load on
31	 * Proxmox by the server count for every admin with this tab open) and there is
32	 * no live connection/session count anywhere on the platform (RCON can fetch a
33	 * Minecraft server's online-player count, but only one server at a time, on
34	 * demand — there is no fleet-wide sweep that samples it). Both are real v2
35	 * candidates, not faked here. See the doc comment on `MonitorFeed.gaps`.
36	 */
